//RS /// D-MEM-COPYSEM1: a plain `loop item in list` (or `loop (index, item) in
//RS /// list`) over a read parameter's list walks the list in place. The loop
//RS /// becomes an index range over the list's length whose item is a read-only
//RS /// alias of its slot, so neither the list nor any item is copied; the
//RS /// two-name form binds the range index itself as `index`. The parameter
//RS /// cannot change while the loop runs, so every alias reads exactly what the
//RS /// copied item would hold. #4318 §4: a stable source (sema proved the body
//RS /// never mentions its root) walks the same way when it is rooted at a local
//RS /// or any parameter. A columnar list (D-SOA1) stores one column per field,
//RS /// so its slots are not places an alias can name; it keeps the
//RS /// gathered-record iteration.
